    entries.compute(k, (key, entry) -> {
        if (entry == null || entry.status() != Status.PENDING) {
            return entry;  // no change — returns false
        }
        transitioned[0] = true;
        return new PendingEntry(entry.planReference(), Status.APPROVED,
                new PlanApproval(entry.planReference(), approvedBy, Instant.now()), null);
    });
    return transitioned[0];
}
```

The `compute()` lambda runs under the segment lock — the read, check, and write are a single atomic operation. The `boolean[]` pattern captures the transition result out of the lambda (lambdas can't assign to local variables).

